# What ./merge.sh writes here, beside it: the results of merging everything in
# input/. All three are derived and are rebuilt byte-identically by the next
# run (SPEC 3.1).
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so they match ONLY this directory. Without it,
# `merged.csv` matches at any depth and swallows
# tests/fixtures/input/merged.csv - the fixture that proves the merge does not
# read its own output back.
/merged.csv
/merge_conflicts.csv
/merge_manifest.json
